{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future","id":151363,"title":"Aberrant: Present or slightly in the future?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-28T09:30:29-07:00","id":151363,"title":"Aberrant: Present or slightly in the future?","content":"The original canon year was 2008, 10 years after the Galatea destruction. Obviously, the base date was reached by 6 years and going.<br /> <br /> Will Aberrant still start in 1998-2008 and go wholly Alternate Timeline or is the base date going to get a bump? Will it be a bump into the present (2014-2016), or near future a la cyberpunk (2020+)? How does updating things affect or not the Aberrant War and other events?<br /> <br /> I'm really curious about how things will turn out or not and would like to hear from other people, be it official or just wild mass guessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T11:13:53-07:00","id":151468,"title":"","content":"I think, though do not know for sure, that they will maintain the &quot;20 minutes in the future&quot; approach and have the game &quot;start&quot; shortly after the new Trinity Continuum launches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T11:42:58-07:00","id":151535,"title":"","content":"I know I've said it before, but I hope Aberrant gets moved to 2023. That way, each of the tree primary lines can start a century apart 1923, 2023, 2123. I like the semetry.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T03:46:39-07:00","id":152309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=151535#post151535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I've said it before, but I hope Aberrant gets moved to 2023. That way, each of the tree primary lines can start a century apart 1923, 2023, 2123. I like the semetry.<br /> <br /> -Slag</div> </div> </div> </div>Having each in a different century as base would be good indeed.<br /> <br /> As an aside, wasn't there talk of the new core book of the Continuum having a modern/present setting of its own? Would like to know if its fact or just fanon so far, as it sounds like it would be awfully close to Aberrant chronologically if it comes to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-29-2014, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T04:04:07-07:00","id":152314,"title":"","content":"Slagheap, the Century theme would be pretty nice.<br /> <br /> I've got no idea about Trinity getting a &quot;modern day&quot; book. I'm not particularly interested in one, since Aberrant pretty much covers that niche - It's either now or 5 minutes into the future, depending on how long you've given it since the Galatea blew up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T07:19:28-07:00","id":152483,"title":"","content":"Aberrant needs the ten year offset between the Galatea explosion and the start of the game &quot;now&quot; time to allow the shiny to wear off the idea of Novas and start the tip-over into cynicism that puts the players at the critical point in time where they can the most good (or evil). It gives just enough time to run through the equivalent of the Golden/Silver age stage so the characters can come in during the Bronze equivalent. Too short a time and the slowly swelling backlash against the Novas would either be too far in the minority to have much influence or there would have to be a tremendous negative reaction right from the start to get to the tip-over point so fast which would make for a completely different tone from not only the original game but also from the comics themselves. Too long a time would make it feel like the situation had stabilized to where the backlash gets disconnected from the elapsed time and something else would have to trigger it to make much sense.<br /> <br /> As long as a similar offset is used the two events can float a little without causing too many problems though there are some constraints if it is to use the &quot;sliding contemporary&quot; style of mainline comics. If the &quot;now&quot; target is 2023, in order for there to be time for the situation to bake to the right point stylistically and not seem overly rushed the Galatea explosion would have to be set somewhere around 2013 which would not be a problem if Aberrant and the new &quot;contemporary&quot; setting in the core book overlap. On the other hand if they do not overlap and the explosion is set for somewhere around 2023 with Aberrant &quot;now&quot; pushed back to 2033 or later instead to allow more time for the contemporary setting to be free of Novas then Aberrant runs the risk of loosing the immediacy of the &quot;5 (or 15) minutes into the future&quot; feel and becoming &quot;near future&quot; scifi, especially since the single power origin (and some other aspects) already pulls toward sci-fi.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what is actually planned, but if they decide to keep the general shape of events and game tone intact from the original game there is some wiggle room but not by much. Who knows, they may even go for something completely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","user":"BC001","date":". 05-29-2014, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T09:05:23-07:00","id":152579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=152309#post152309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having each in a different century as base would be good indeed.<br /> <br /> As an aside, wasn't there talk of the new core book of the Continuum having a modern/present setting of its own? Would like to know if its fact or just fanon so far, as it sounds like it would be awfully close to Aberrant chronologically if it comes to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's right on our <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule\" target=\"_blank\">current projects</a> page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>: A new edition of the fan-favorite Trinity Universe, the Trinity Continuum depicts a world of heroes willing to jump into action, to right wrongs, stand up to tyranny, and make the world a better place. This rulebook contains the core rules for playing games set in the Continuum, which will be the basis for further rulebooks such as <b>The Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b>. In addition, it contains a modern-day action-adventure setting where teams of daring men and women confront corruption, solve problems, and defeat the bizarre. Also contains rules for playing Talents, those people who display extraordinary skill or luck. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=152314#post152314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got no idea about Trinity getting a &quot;modern day&quot; book. I'm not particularly interested in one, since Aberrant pretty much covers that niche - It's either now or 5 minutes into the future, depending on how long you've given it since the Galatea blew up.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I certainly have no issue with anyone who wants to play Aberrant in the modern day, they're different books because they're different genres and focus on different character types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 05-29-2014, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T08:05:31-07:00","id":153849,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I was assuming that the games would still have the two phases of Human and Nova in character creation, making the &quot;Normals&quot; book superflous. The Trinity Continuum book work as the WoD 2.0 core book, then? Will it include any of the &quot;specials&quot; of the Adventure! era? The original Aberrant started &quot;Now&quot; (Galatea was 1998, the game came out 1999) and then fast forwarded a decade. So when does Aberrant start?<br /> <br /> And thanks for chipping in Ian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T10:30:58-07:00","id":153969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=153849#post153849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I was assuming that the games would still have the two phases of Human and Nova in character creation</div> </div> </div> </div>Have I said anything which indicates otherwise?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , making the &quot;Normals&quot; book superflous. </div> </div> </div>Talents are not baseline humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T13:39:04-07:00","id":154152,"title":"","content":"Making no assumptions on my part of what the books will eventually contain, it will be interesting, fun, and very wonderful to see what you all have cooked up -- once everything is written and released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T16:56:41-07:00","id":154298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=153969#post153969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Talents are not baseline humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating - what will they be, then?<br /> <br /> As an aside, talks of a post-Inspired, pre-Novas contemporary setting makes me think a lot of <a href=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/7/71975/2602395-planetary_26.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Planetary</a>, a bit of <a href=\"http://www.freakangels.com/?p=23\" target=\"_blank\">FreakAngels</a>.<br /> How appropriate/close would either be as inspiration/parallel to what we can expect from the rulebook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-30-2014, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T18:53:12-07:00","id":154425,"title":"","content":"I believe &quot;Talents&quot; is the Trinity Continuum word for what &quot;Daredevils&quot; are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T21:46:28-07:00","id":154511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=154425#post154425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe &quot;Talents&quot; is the Trinity Continuum word for what &quot;Daredevils&quot; are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think i heard something like that somewhere but would like to wait and see - among other reasons, because i don't really see much reason for one kind of inspired to be out and about and the others to simply disappear like mist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T03:10:32-07:00","id":154636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=154425#post154425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe &quot;Talents&quot; is the Trinity Continuum word for what &quot;Daredevils&quot; are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know i missed some of the late game metadiscussion on what the actual splats are and how they work in the back end, but Mesmerists were ProtoPsions and Stalwarts were ProtoNovas. Daredevils were their own thing, right? What are paramorphs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T08:52:54-07:00","id":154873,"title":"","content":"While I ran with the idea in my game that paramorphs represented the potential &quot;evolution&quot; of daredevils (albeit <i>incredibly rare</i> potential), officially I believe that paramorphs are <i>not</i> directly related to any other Inspired. They are unique, apart from all the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:29:07-07:00","id":155026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=154511#post154511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think i heard something like that somewhere but would like to wait and see - among other reasons, because i don't really see much reason for one kind of inspired to be out and about and the others to simply disappear like mist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like the Aberrant and Trinity eras had more than one sort of Inspired!<br /> <br /> Oh wait","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T12:13:26-07:00","id":155089,"title":"","content":"Teehee.<br /> <br /> I suppose, if we wanted to get nitpicky, they <i>did</i> have more than one type of Inspired... but honestly, they were incredibly focused on a single type. Eximorphs in Trinity are either insane or very distant, and they are universally rare in the setting. Likewise, psychomorphs in Aberrant are extremely uncommon -- and those that do exist generally think they are Novas, due to Utopia's PR campaign, unless they happened to be brought into Pandora. Either way, it probably wouldn't be too far out to assume that there is a good 500-to-1 ratio in these settings between the &quot;primary&quot; Inspired and the &quot;other&quot; Inspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T15:43:05-07:00","id":156945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=154636#post154636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know i missed some of the late game metadiscussion on what the actual splats are and how they work in the back end, but Mesmerists were ProtoPsions and Stalwarts were ProtoNovas. Daredevils were their own thing, right? What are paramorphs?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two schools of thought on this: one is that paramorphs are <b>Adventure!</b>\u2019s daredevils and whatever they might evolve into; the other is that paramorphs are time travelers \u2014 and that the plural form isn\u2019t applicable, as there\u2019s only one known to exist: Max Mercer. The former theory says that what daredevils do is a low-level, subconscious manipulation of the timestream; the latter theory says that daredevils excel the way they do strictly due to the heroic nature of the genre.<br /> <br /> So really, the better question isn\u2019t \u201cwhat are paramorphs?\u201d but rather \u201cwhat are daredevils?\u201d Thematically, daredevils are people with no powers per se; just extraordinary skill and a tendency to defy the odds. Indiana Jones, Batman, and Captain Kirk are examples of daredevils. The key issue is whether that tendency to defy the odds is strictly a genre convention, or if it\u2019s a legitimate in-setting power in its own right. That is, whether daredevils are extraordinarily competent baselines, or if they\u2019re paramorphs. <br /> <br /> Stalwarts, meanwhile, were what <b>Aberrant</b> calls \u201cstealth novas\u201d: novas without any flashy Quantum Powers or blatantly obvious high-level Mega-Attributes who instead relied almost exclusively on the equivalent of some of the more subtle Enhancements. (<b>Adventure!</b>\u2019s Dynamic Knacks are always about enhancing one\u2019s Attributes in some way.) And mesmerists are essentially the same thing as <b>Aberrant</b>\u2019s psiads: not as powerful as psions, but considerably more diverse.<br /> <br /> And coming back to daredevils and paramorphs: if they\u2019re the same thing, then Max Mercer is the only known \u201cevolved daredevil\u201d; if they\u2019re different things, Max Mercer is the only known paramorph. Either way, we\u2019ve got a sample of one in terms of what paramorphs are truly capable of. I\u2019m hoping that Trinity Continuum will eventually open up time travelers like Max Mercer as a playable option: but if so, it should be after <b>\u00c6on</b>, <b>Aberrant</b>, and <b>Adventure!</b> are out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-02-2014, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T21:43:46-07:00","id":158695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=156945#post156945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are two schools of thought on this: one is that paramorphs are <b>Adventure!</b>\u2019s daredevils and whatever they might evolve into; the other is that paramorphs are time travelers \u2014 and that the plural form isn\u2019t applicable, as there\u2019s only one known to exist: Max Mercer. The former theory says that what daredevils do is a low-level, subconscious manipulation of the timestream; the latter theory says that daredevils excel the way they do strictly due to the heroic nature of the genre.<br /> <br /> So really, the better question isn\u2019t \u201cwhat are paramorphs?\u201d but rather \u201cwhat are daredevils?\u201d Thematically, daredevils are people with no powers per se; just extraordinary skill and a tendency to defy the odds. Indiana Jones, Batman, and Captain Kirk are examples of daredevils. The key issue is whether that tendency to defy the odds is strictly a genre convention, or if it\u2019s a legitimate in-setting power in its own right. That is, whether daredevils are extraordinarily competent baselines, or if they\u2019re paramorphs.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or perhaps Daredevils a combination of the two. Just as there's a metaphysical cause for genre conventions in setting Z-rays and their descendants perhaps humans are naturally capable of such things they just need Z-rays to be there to be bent. Much like a swimmer needs water to swim,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T23:00:21-07:00","id":158749,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting analogy. It's as good a theory as any -- especially when there aren't clear-cut answers for Daredevils. It's kind of hard to say that Telluric energy isn't it's own energy (like a confusion of both Noetic and Quantum energies) when you can put a colander on a Daredevil's head, extract their Inspiration, and gain measurable and quantifiable amounts of Telluric energy from them to put in a battery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:56:10-07:00","id":159160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=158749#post158749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting analogy. It's as good a theory as any -- especially when there aren't clear-cut answers for Daredevils. It's kind of hard to say that Telluric energy isn't it's own energy (like a confusion of both Noetic and Quantum energies) when you can put a colander on a Daredevil's head, extract their Inspiration, and gain measurable and quantifiable amounts of Telluric energy from them to put in a battery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention the fact mega-strength in normal people can be induced through nova hormones or that is even possible (though possibly damaging) to transfer quantum powers to non-novas for some time brings with it some implication that <b>all human beings</b> may have some incomplete/limited compatibility with the quantum field novas manipulate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:23:32-07:00","id":159188,"title":"","content":"I used these ideas for my Adventure!/Aberrant/Trinity game. I ran with the idea presented in Trinity that no Quantum-manipulating races had been found, except for humans. I decided that, due to the effects of Hammersmith's experiments, the Telluric energy that traveled <i>back</i> in time from his device's activation retroactively &quot;primed&quot; humanity to channel Telluric (and Quantum, and to an extent Noetic) energy in ways no other species could. Which led to the Doyen getting involved.<br /> <br /> The Hammersmith experiment got their curiosity.<br /> <br /> The Galatea explosion got their attention.<br /> <br /> The Aberrant War and exodus earned their terror.<br /> <br /> The Trinity era saw their wrath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T11:19:07-07:00","id":159220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=159188#post159188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used these ideas for my Adventure!/Aberrant/Trinity game. I ran with the idea presented in Trinity that no Quantum-manipulating races had been found, except for humans. I decided that, due to the effects of Hammersmith's experiments, the Telluric energy that traveled <i>back</i> in time from his device's activation retroactively &quot;primed&quot; humanity to channel Telluric (and Quantum, and to an extent Noetic) energy in ways no other species could. Which led to the Doyen getting involved.<br /> <br /> The Hammersmith experiment got their curiosity.<br /> <br /> The Galatea explosion got their attention.<br /> <br /> The Aberrant War and exodus earned their terror.<br /> <br /> The Trinity era saw their wrath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice way to set up it all, at least.<br /> <br /> Last time i actually played with Aberrant backstory was in a quite different setting that expanded from a New Gods-esque chronicle i played with a group of friends. In that version the Hammersmith experiment actually touched the unconscious thoughts of an extradimensional entity that entered Earth and tweaked a few humans here and there through the timestream, while hiding its tracks in the temporal movements of Mercer and others, to serve as its future defenders/soldiers when the enemies it was hiding from eventually found it.<br /> <br /> Much to its misfortune, the one that eventually came after it were a whole new set of enemies it wasn't even aware of possessing, descended of previously abandoned soldiers/allies of its part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:07:53-07:00","id":161719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=158695#post158695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or perhaps Daredevils a combination of the two. Just as there's a metaphysical cause for genre conventions in setting Z-rays and their descendants perhaps humans are naturally capable of such things they just need Z-rays to be there to be bent. Much like a swimmer needs water to swim,</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not a combination of the two; that\u2019s the latter option (that a daredevil\u2019s tendency to defy the odds has an in-setting explanation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=158749#post158749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting analogy. It's as good a theory as any -- especially when there aren't clear-cut answers for Daredevils. It's kind of hard to say that Telluric energy isn't it's own energy (like a confusion of both Noetic and Quantum energies) when you can put a colander on a Daredevil's head, extract their Inspiration, and gain measurable and quantifiable amounts of Telluric energy from them to put in a battery.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Adventure!</b> had some flat-out contradictory elements in it, such as the contradiction between this and the statement that Dramatic Editing isn\u2019t an in-setting thing. Part of the issue is that <b>Adventure!</b> was trying to squeeze a lot of options into very little space; so it tended to conflate things that ought not be conflated. One such conflation is Inspiration (a metagaming currency intended to facilitate genre conventions; mainly through paying for Dramatic Edits, which are explicitly presented as metagaming tools and specifically denied being in-game reality warping) and Telluric Energy (itself a conflation of Quantum and Noetic energies, reflecting that era\u2019s imprecise understanding of the exotic energies that Hammersmith unleashed; and definitely an in-setting thing).<br /> <br /> IMC, I address this by giving the Inspired up to two fuel stats: all three have Inspiration; but mesmerists and stalwarts supplement this with a separate Telluric Energy rating, representing Noetic Energy (if you\u2019re a mesmerist) or Quantum Energy (if you\u2019re a stalwart).<br /> <br /> Note: IMHO, the most important part of the above quote is \u201cit\u2019s as good a theory as any \u2014 especially when there aren\u2019t clear-cut answers for daredevils.\u201d Bear in mind that TC isn\u2019t TU; and even if TU settled the question (which it didn\u2019t), there\u2019s no guarantee that TC will settle the question in the same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=159160#post159160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention the fact mega-strength in normal people can be induced through nova hormones or that is even possible (though possibly damaging) to transfer quantum powers to non-novas for some time brings with it some implication that <b>all human beings</b> may have some incomplete/limited compatibility with the quantum field novas manipulate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no problem with the notion that Quantum Energies can be artificially implanted in people who have no innate ability to generate or manipulate Quantum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-07-2014, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T11:52:19-07:00","id":161890,"title":"","content":"Exquisite!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T21:12:42-07:00","id":162190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=161719#post161719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem with the notion that Quantum Energies can be artificially implanted in people who have no innate ability to generate or manipulate Quantum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throwing light at the blind won't on itself make them see. Inserting an energy in itself only makes you a battery - <b>if</b> you are capable of collecting it. <b>Wielding</b> it is a whole different and quite interesting on itself matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T06:00:44-07:00","id":162370,"title":"","content":"That's where the laser eyes and power gauntlets come in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:06:46-07:00","id":163935,"title":"","content":"Future dates you always run into, sooner or later, alternate histories can be very fun if you ask me. 2023 ain't <i>that</i> far off, but I see no reason to change the original timeline unless you REALLY want to play some funky timey whimey symmetry thingsies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Man's unfailing capacity to believe what he prefers to be true rather than what the evidence shows to be likely and possible has always astounded me. We long for a caring Universe which will save us from our childish mistakes, and in the face of mountains of evidence to the contrary we will pin all our hopes on the slimmest of doubts. God has not been proven not to exist, therefore he must exist.</i> <b>--Academician Prokhor Zakharov</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3246-galaxy-master-zhad","name":"Galaxy Master Zhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T17:00:25-07:00","id":164207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=161719#post161719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Adventure!</b> had some flat-out contradictory elements in it, such as the contradiction between this and the statement that Dramatic Editing isn\u2019t an in-setting thing. Part of the issue is that <b>Adventure!</b> was trying to squeeze a lot of options into very little space; so it tended to conflate things that ought not be conflated. One such conflation is Inspiration (a metagaming currency intended to facilitate genre conventions; mainly through paying for Dramatic Edits, which are explicitly presented as metagaming tools and specifically denied being in-game reality warping) and Telluric Energy (itself a conflation of Quantum and Noetic energies, reflecting that era\u2019s imprecise understanding of the exotic energies that Hammersmith unleashed; and definitely an in-setting thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally the first thing we did on systems team was make a decision on this very topic. <i>Literally</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T19:21:58-07:00","id":170331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/151363-aberrant-present-or-slightly-in-the-future?p=161719#post161719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s not a combination of the two; that\u2019s the latter option (that a daredevil\u2019s tendency to defy the odds has an in-setting explanation).</div> </div> </div> </div>what I mean is rather than assuming that Daredevils are a third type of superbeing they are the natural state of humans. Anyone could be one with enough training like being a doctor. Zrays are just sort of a requirement of the situation like water to swim or a certain level of technology to be a computer technician.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T06:55:46-07:00","id":170677,"title":"","content":"Regarding the present/near future thing, my own ideal setting for Aberrant would be... 2008. Or maybe the year the game comes out, but the key point being, it's not the future at all. It is, however, 10 years after novas came onto the scene. <br /> <br /> What's fun about this is you can make a setting that still *feels* like the future, but which is actually the world of today (or even a couple years ago), sent down a dramatically different path by the existence of superhumans. <br /> <br /> My ideal setting for Aberrant is one where N-Day still occurred in 1998, and we are now living years later, in the very different world that resulted. The Twin Towers are still standing, but of course the War on Terror not only still exists, but has much higher stakes following the Sao Paulo bombing. The OpNet has created a tightly controlled corporate alternative to the low-speed, low-regulation internet, which is now only used by privacy nuts, copyright pirates and other more sordid criminals. And of course the Democratic primary is drawing all sorts of interesting commentary, with a three way race to pick between a black man, a white woman, and the first serious nova candidate...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T21:28:51-07:00","id":199648,"title":"","content":"Truth be told, i'm more curious about what direction might be taken or not than focused in either, be it future or alternate timeline, having Aberrant back in the 'hood is more than enough to make me happy. That and the fact i would like to know more on the basic scenario of TC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}